{"base_rate":0.13438735177865613,"brier":0.07250698287220028,"bss":0.37669897036440136,"bss_hi":0.47094568816431087,"bss_lo":0.27417007317609776,"chart":{"base":[236.3,132.4],"fp":[191.7,190.7],"lead":"62,265.1 272,251.6 482,219.4 692,167.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.38 — higher than 66% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +26pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 76% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 55% → rained 59%"},"rel":"68.9,456.7 407.8,213.1"},"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.05320158102766799,"ess":361.8856518572473,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nogales</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nogales rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (78%), believe about\n<b>59%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 759 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNOGALES INTL AP, 15.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.38, ranked 45 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(23&ndash;84) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>529</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nogales</b> <span class=\"muted\">MX</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.38</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>23&ndash;84\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>759 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nogales &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nogales\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.48850661625709,379.9357277882798 84.86769230769231,330.6666666666667 170.72105263157897,228.73684210526318 333.88710526315793,70.68421052631578 333.88710526315793,128.15789473684214 170.72105263157897,300.57894736842104 84.86769230769231,372.6666666666667 58.48850661625709,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"333.0830039525692\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"333.0830039525692\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.48850661625709,381.3119092627599 84.86769230769231,326.0 170.72105263157897,171.26315789473682 333.88710526315793,166.47368421052633\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 529 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.48850661625709\" cy=\"381.3119092627599\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"84.86769230769231\" cy=\"326.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"170.72105263157897\" cy=\"171.26315789473682\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"333.88710526315793\" cy=\"166.47368421052633\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(13%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nogales the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.51) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.14).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.143</td><td class='num'>14.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'>0.463</td><td class='num'>2.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>0.471</td><td class='num'>4.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'>0.506</td><td class='num'>4.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":31.30862,"lon":-110.94217,"n":759,"n_cities":134,"name":"Nogales","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.001379962192816635,"n":529,"obs":0.001890359168241966,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18399999999999977,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.0758974358974359,"n":78,"obs":0.15384615384615385,"sig":true},{"hi":0.49200000000000044,"lo":0.18399999999999977,"mean":0.318421052631579,"n":76,"obs":0.5789473684210527,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.49200000000000044,"mean":0.779342105263158,"n":76,"obs":0.5921052631578947,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":15.4,"provisional":false,"rank":45,"rank_hi":84.02499999999998,"rank_lo":23.0,"reliability":0.010931314002768177,"resolution":0.053042101945363296,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"nogales","station":"NOGALES INTL AP","timezone":"America/Hermosillo"}